# =====================================================================================
#  Cab Eye — .gitignore
#
#  Rule of thumb: commit the SOURCE, ignore anything a build or a tool regenerates,
#  and ignore anything that is specific to one machine.
# =====================================================================================

# --- Gradle / Android / Java build output ------------------------------------------
# These are rebuilt every time you run gradlew or the install script. The release APK
# alone is ~11 MB and changes on every build, so it must never be committed.
build/
.gradle/
.kotlin/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class
*.jar
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
local.properties

# --- Backend data (accounts, sessions, rider memory) ----------------------------------
# Real people's phone numbers and trip history. Never commit it.
backend/data/
data/

# --- Signing keys --------------------------------------------------------------------
# A keystore signs your app as YOU. If one leaks, someone else can publish updates that
# phones will accept as genuine. Never commit these, even for a hobby project.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# --- Secrets and machine-specific config ---------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.properties

# --- Tools that are downloaded, not authored -----------------------------------------
# ngrok is a 33 MB third-party binary. share-with-friends.ps1 already tells you to
# download it yourself and drop it next to the script, so git does not need a copy.
ngrok.exe
ngrok.yml

# --- Run logs ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# share-with-friends.ps1 rewrites this on every run; it is a record of one session,
# not part of the project.
*.log

# --- IDE / editor --------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- OS clutter ----------------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# --- Database (H2 on the laptop) ------------------------------------------------------
# backend/data/ is already ignored above; these catch a database file anywhere else, e.g.
# if the backend is ever started from a different folder.
*.mv.db
*.trace.db
*.lock.db
*.json.imported

# --- Admin / alert secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Admin password, Telegram bot token, Gmail app password. The .example file (no real
# values) IS committed so others know what to fill in.
cabeye-secrets.properties
cabeye-secrets*.properties
!cabeye-secrets.example.properties

# --- Identity documents used for testing ---------------------------------------------
# Driving licences / RC books (DigiLocker PDFs, screenshots) are other people's personal
# data. Keep them in a folder named private/ or test-documents/ — never committed.
private/
test-documents/
*DrivingLicen*
*digilocker*
*DigiLocker*

# --- Android Studio extras -----------------------------------------------------------
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.hprof
